Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Chaotian Jing &lt;chaotian.jing@mediatek.com&gt;  Change-Id: Ifc57b2662e17563badf521e3259cc71dba119fc3 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/423912 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="423912" owner_email="djkurtz@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/12/423912/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5f680fede5cb4effa86243f51edfdea09db4d975" commit="323fe59f7058bc12476ffc2d6d885f9e8140fa40" commit_message="power/skylake: Add option to reset pmic using LDO_EN  Add a config option that can be used by chipset to provide PMIC reset using LDO_EN. This is required for ensuring that the AP is power cycled properly. Implement the special pmic reset for skylake chipsets.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:61883 BRANCH=None TEST=Verified that reboot on EC console resets the AP and does not get stuck in G3 on poppy.  Change-Id: I5f680fede5cb4effa86243f51edfdea09db4d975 Signed-off-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/431192 Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="431192" owner_email="furquan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/92/431192/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I0a2b052790fec2d55417e32f5aea53a7438a038f" commit="05613c118e7753a23988dc2d6468a76c65109ad6" commit_message="poppy: Select CONFIG_CHIPSET_HAS_PLATFORM_PMIC_RESET  Also program EC_PLATFORM_RST as an out signal from the EC.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:61883 BRANCH=None TEST=Verified that reboot on EC console works fine for poppy. Board is no longer stuck in G3.  Change-Id: I0a2b052790fec2d55417e32f5aea53a7438a038f Signed-off-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/431193 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="431193" owner_email="furquan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/93/431193/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I41486e6050727ca822a27054244da3fed5ee3b7a" commit="c5eb322d3db6a6b639eafde504827ed410b674c0" commit_message="eve: Select CONFIG_CHIPSET_HAS_PLATFORM_PMIC_RESET  Also program EC_PLATFORM_RST as an out signal from the EC.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:61883 BRANCH=None TEST=Compiles successfully for eve.  Change-Id: I41486e6050727ca822a27054244da3fed5ee3b7a Signed-off-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/431194 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="431194" owner_email="furquan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/94/431194/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I72a53f15ddc2c64a3b117a3be45eb3b3ae5ed1f4" commit="1ecfce1e4e730f984ef472acf9a0164554b3148d" commit_message="UPSTREAM: random: initialize the non-blocking pool via add_hwgenerator_randomness()  If we have a hardware RNG and are using the in-kernel rngd, we should use this to initialize the non-blocking pool so that getrandom(2) doesn't block unnecessarily.  BUG=chromium:673183 TEST=none  Signed-off-by: Theodore Ts'o &lt;tytso@mit.edu&gt; Signed-off-by: Greg Kroah-Hartman &lt;gregkh@linuxfoundation.org&gt;  (cherry picked from commit f41fc0bfede5bbeca4f09d75c76c4db5d6c0d2ee) Signed-off-by: Chung-yih Wang &lt;cywang@google.com&gt;  Change-Id: I72a53f15ddc2c64a3b117a3be45eb3b3ae5ed1f4 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/429350 Commit-Ready: Chung-yih Wang &lt;cywang@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Chung-yih Wang &lt;cywang@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Luigi Semenzato &lt;semenzato@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="429350" owner_email="cywang@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/50/429350/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I31541b5c0febdac7914a9cdc1c22ec137fb06e03" commit="496c957603a7c37955bcd741d4766f618ebd8253" commit_message="CHROMIUM: tpm-rng: Make hwrng working  The patch fixes two issues to make hwrng working for ChromeOS. First, make sure that the tpm-tis module is initialized before tpm-rng. From the latency measurement listed below, it takes around 27ms for each rng_get_data call to TPM module to generate a 64-byte randomness on Ultima with Infineon TPM 1.2. The tpm-rng module makes a rng_get_data call in add_early_randomness in registration of hwrng which add a 27ms latency to the kernel boot time. Second, the quality of randomness of tpm-rng is set(default is off) in order to create additional kernel thread(named hwrng) to keep pumping data from TPM as one of the linux-rng sources for input_pool continuously. The value of the 'quality' is used for the ratio 'quality/1024', i.e. 1000/1024 here, of randomness bits generated by TPM to be added into the linux-rng entropy. For example, from the sequences of rng_get_data calls listed below, the rng_get_data calls in hwrng_fillfn function are in kthread hwrng which won't block the kernel boot up at all. The nonblocking pool got initialized after two fillups(add_early_randomness and the first rng_get_data call in hwrng_fillfn), then the hwrng kthread keeps filling up the input_pool until the entropy of input_pool is larger than 'random_write_wakeup_bits' or 896(28*32) bits(which is completed in another four rng_get_data calls in hwrng_fill). The seventh rng_get_data call(@2.081762) is triggered by borging ssl patch which makes the entropy got a bit lower by getrandom calls. In other words, if the available entropy drops to zero and no other rng sources available, tpm-rng should be able to fillup the entropy with four rng_get_data calls(1000 = 4 * (32 * 8 * 1000/1024) &gt; 896) with rng_buffer_size of 32 bytes.  === the trace of rng_get_data calls on ultima===  2017-01-20T14:25:22.814436+08:00 ERR kernel: [    0.755589] ===add_early_randomness before rng_get_data 2017-01-20T14:25:22.814442+08:00 ERR kernel: [    0.780133] ===add_early_randomness after rng_get_data 2017-01-20T14:25:22.814516+08:00 ERR kernel: [    0.782590] ===hwrng_fillfn before rng_get_data 2017-01-20T14:25:22.814539+08:00 ERR kernel: [    0.806457] ===hwrng_fillfn after rng_get_data 2017-01-20T14:25:22.814546+08:00 NOTICE kernel: [    0.806523] random: nonblocking pool is initialized 2017-01-20T14:25:22.814551+08:00 ERR kernel: [    0.806533] ===hwrng_fillfn before rng_get_data 2017-01-20T14:25:22.815692+08:00 ERR kernel: [    0.836772] ===hwrng_fillfn after rng_get_data 2017-01-20T14:25:22.815699+08:00 ERR kernel: [    0.836796] ===hwrng_fillfn before rng_get_data 2017-01-20T14:25:22.815756+08:00 ERR kernel: [    0.866494] ===hwrng_fillfn after rng_get_data 2017-01-20T14:25:22.815762+08:00 ERR kernel: [    0.866513] ===hwrng_fillfn before rng_get_data 2017-01-20T14:25:22.815775+08:00 ERR kernel: [    0.896360] ===hwrng_fillfn after rng_get_data 2017-01-20T14:25:22.815788+08:00 ERR kernel: [    0.896378] ===hwrng_fillfn before rng_get_data 2017-01-20T14:25:22.815797+08:00 ERR kernel: [    0.926356] ===hwrng_fillfn after rng_get_data 2017-01-20T14:25:23.043052+08:00 ERR kernel: [    2.081762] ===hwrng_fillfn before rng_get_data 2017-01-20T14:25:23.067059+08:00 ERR kernel: [    2.105352] ===hwrng_fillfn after rng_get_data 2017-01-20T14:26:21.090057+08:00 ERR kernel: [   60.227756] ===hwrng_fillfn before rng_get_data 2017-01-20T14:26:21.114048+08:00 ERR kernel: [   60.251414] ===hwrng_fillfn after rng_get_data 2017-01-20T14:28:31.180226+08:00 ERR kernel: [  190.312773] ===hwrng_fillfn before rng_get_data 2017-01-20T14:28:31.207700+08:00 ERR kernel: [  190.340068] BUG=chromium:673183 TEST=emerge-ultima chromeos-kernel-3_18; update kernel;     test_that DUT_IP BootPerfServerCrosPerf and have good test results  Change-Id: I31541b5c0febdac7914a9cdc1c22ec137fb06e03 Signed-off-by: Chung-yih Wang &lt;cywang@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/427621 " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="427621" owner_email="cywang@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/21/427621/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If52d4505f933655deb4f180e105eff545e24b470" commit="62a2856eeeaa2d2ce0b908216173cef7ae0ec431" commit_message="dbus: login_manager: Add SetArcCpuRestriction  This method will be used to deprioritize the Android container when there isn't any user interaction.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:60946 TEST=chromeos-login and chrome build when using this constant.  Change-Id: If52d4505f933655deb4f180e105eff545e24b470 Signed-off-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/422470 Commit-Ready: Yusuke Sato &lt;yusukes@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Yusuke Sato &lt;yusukes@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromiu